  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Meghri BCP Modernisation Project - Project Coordination Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Meghri Border Crossing Point (BCP) Modernisation Project, financed by the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD), aims to enhance the safety, security, and efficiency of the Meghri BCP in Armenia. A sovereign loan of up to EUR 10.63 million from EBRD, complemented by a EUR 10.52 million investment grant from the EU Neighbourhood Investment Platform, supports the project. The Republic of Armenia, represented by the Ministry of Finance, is the borrower, and the State Revenue Committee (SRC) is the implementing agency. The UNDP, starting in June 2024, will assist the SRC in ensuring compliance with EBRD policies, environmental and social standards, and efficient project execution. This initiative is expected to significantly boost regional cooperation and economic activities, and will be specifically responsible for the following:1.	Capacity building for the SRC&#x2019;s Project Implementation Unit (PIU);2.	Assistance with contract implementation;3.	Coordination of all Stakeholders and support in implementation;4.	Assistance with compliance &amp; reporting obligations under the financing documents; and5.	Environmental and social implementation support.</narrative>
  </description>
